s="mat-mdc-button-persistent-ripple mdc-icon-button__ripple"></span><gem-icon _ngcontent-ng-c2208423640="" _nghost-ng-c3459726168=""><mat-icon _ngcontent-ng-c3459726168="" role="img" class="mat-icon notranslate lm-icon-l lumi-symbols mat-ligature-font mat-icon-no-color ng-star-inserted" aria-hidden="true" data-mat-icon-type="font" data-mat-icon-name="copy" data-mat-icon-namespace="lumi-symbols" fonticon="copy"></mat-icon><!----><!----><!----></gem-icon><!----><span class="mat-focus-indicator"></span><span class="mat-mdc-button-touch-target"></span></button><!----><!----></gem-icon-button><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><!----><!----></div><!----><pre _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" class="ng-tns-c2911514074-35"><code _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" role="text" data-test-id="code-content" class="code-container formatted ng-tns-c2911514074-35">npx npkill
</code></pre><!----></div></div></div><!----><!----><!----></code-block><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></response-element><p data-path-to-node="7,0,2"><i data-path-to-node="7,0,2" data-index-in-node="0">(This will list all <code data-path-to-node="7,0,2" data-index-in-node="20">node_modules</code> folders on your drive and let you delete them safely with the spacebar. It won't break your code; you can always re-run <code data-path-to-node="7,0,2" data-index-in-node="153">npm install</code> later if you open the project again).</i></p></li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node="8">üìÅ NPM Cache accumulation</h3><p data-path-to-node="9">NPM keeps a copy of every package you have ever downloaded so it can install them faster next time. Over months of development, this cache grows massive.</p><ul data-path-to-node="10"><li><p data-path-to-node="10,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="10,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Fix:</b> Clear your NPM cache by running:</p><response-element class="" ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><code-block _nghost-ng-c2911514074="" class="ng-tns-c2911514074-36 enable-luminous-code-block ng-star-inserted" style=""><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" class="code-block ng-tns-c2911514074-36 ng-animate-disabled ng-trigger ng-trigger-codeBlockRevealAnimation" jslog="223238;track:impression,attention;BardVeMetadataKey:[[&quot;r_28039488fb993922&quot;,&quot;c_600683a3d3dbb7f3&quot;,null,&quot;rc_0123e6e0691a8c0c&quot;,null,null,&quot;en&quot;,null,1,null,null,1,0]]" data-hveid="0" decode-data-ved="1" data-ved="0CAAQhtANahcKEwjlssaSjMiVAxUAAAAAHQAAAAAQKg" style="display: block;"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" class="formatted-code-block-internal-container ng-tns-c2911514074-36"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" class="animated-opacity ng-tns-c2911514074-36"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" class="code-block-decoration header-formatted gds-emphasized-body-m ng-tns-c2911514074-36 ng-star-inserted" style=""><span _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" class="ng-tns-c2911514074-36">Bash</span><div _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" class="buttons ng-tns-c2911514074-36 ng-star-inserted"><gem-icon-button _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" tabindex="-1" type="onSurface" size="small" fonticonname="arrow_circle_down" theme="lm" arialabel="Download code" gemtooltip="Download code" class="mat-mdc-tooltip-trigger download-button ng-tns-c2911514074-36 gem-button gem-button-badge-size-small gem-button-size-small gem-button-type-on-surface lm-enabled is-mobile ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c2208423640="" aria-describedby="cdk-describedby-message-ng-1-15" cdk-describedby-host="ng-1"><!----><!----><button _ngcontent-ng-c2208423640="" maticonbutton="" matbadgeposition="after" class="mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-button-base mat-badge mat-unthemed mat-badge-overlap mat-badge-above mat-badge-after mat-badge-small mat-badge-hidden ng-star-inserted" mat-ripple-loader-uninitialized="" mat-ripple-loader-class-name="mat-mdc-button-ripple" mat-ripple-loader-centered="" aria-label="Download code" jslog="305704;track:generic_click,impression"><span class="mat-mdc-button-persistent-ripple mdc-icon-button__ripple"></span><gem-icon _ngcontent-ng-c2208423640="" _nghost-ng-c3459726168=""><mat-icon _ngcontent-ng-c3459726168="" role="img" class="mat-icon notranslate lm-icon-l lumi-symbols mat-ligature-font mat-icon-no-color ng-star-inserted" aria-hidden="true" data-mat-icon-type="font" data-mat-icon-name="arrow_circle_down" data-mat-icon-namespace="lumi-symbols" fonticon="arrow_circle_down"></mat-icon><!----><!----><!----></gem-icon><!----><span class="mat-focus-indicator"></span><span class="mat-mdc-button-touch-target"></span></button><!----><!----></gem-icon-button><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><gem-icon-button _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" tabindex="-1" type="onSurface" size="small" fonticonname="copy" theme="lm" arialabel="Copy code" gemtooltip="Copy code" data-test-id="gem-copy-button" class="mat-mdc-tooltip-trigger copy-button ng-tns-c2911514074-36 gem-button gem-button-badge-size-small gem-button-size-small gem-button-type-on-surface lm-enabled is-mobile ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c2208423640="" aria-describedby="cdk-describedby-message-ng-1-16" cdk-describedby-host="ng-1"><!----><!----><button _ngcontent-ng-c2208423640="" maticonbutton="" matbadgeposition="after" class="mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-button-base mat-badge mat-unthemed mat-badge-overlap mat-badge-above mat-badge-after mat-badge-small mat-badge-hidden ng-star-inserted" mat-ripple-loader-uninitialized="" mat-ripple-loader-class-name="mat-mdc-button-ripple" mat-ripple-loader-centered="" aria-label="Copy code" jslog="179062;track:generic_click,impression;BardVeMetadataKey:[[&quot;r_28039488fb993922&quot;,&quot;c_600683a3d3dbb7f3&quot;,null,&quot;rc_0123e6e0691a8c0c&quot;,null,null,&quot;en&quot;,null,1,null,null,1,0]];mutable:true"><span class="mat-mdc-button-persistent-ripple mdc-icon-button__ripple"></span><gem-icon _ngcontent-ng-c2208423640="" _nghost-ng-c3459726168=""><mat-icon _ngcontent-ng-c3459726168="" role="img" class="mat-icon notranslate lm-icon-l lumi-symbols mat-ligature-font mat-icon-no-color ng-star-inserted" aria-hidden="true" data-mat-icon-type="font" data-mat-icon-name="copy" data-mat-icon-namespace="lumi-symbols" fonticon="copy"></mat-icon><!----><!----><!----></gem-icon><!----><span class="mat-focus-indicator"></span><span class="mat-mdc-button-touch-target"></span></button><!----><!----></gem-icon-button><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><!----><!----></div><!----><pre _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" class="ng-tns-c2911514074-36"><code _ngcontent-ng-c2911514074="" role="text" data-test-id="code-content" class="code-container formatted ng-tns-c2911514074-36">npm cache clean --force
</code></pre><!----></div></div></div><!----><!----><!----></code-block><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></response-element></li></ul><h2 data-path-to-node="12">2. The Database Culprit (MongoDB)</h2><h3 data-path-to-node="13">üìä MongoDB Journal Files</h3><p data-path-to-node="14">By default, MongoDB allocates large files called <b data-path-to-node="14" data-index-in-node="49">journal files</b> to ensure data recovery in case of a crash. If your local MongoDB server is constantly running in the background, its data directory (usually in <code data-path-to-node="14" data-index-in-node="208">C:\data\db</code> or <code data-path-to-node="14" data-index-in-node="222">C:\Program Files\MongoDB</code>) can balloon in size, even if you don't have much data in your collections.</p><ul data-path-to-node="15"><li><p data-path-to-node="15,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="15,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">The Fix:</b> You can compress your database or restrict storage size in your <code data-path-to-node="15,0,0" data-index-in-node="73">mongod.cfg</code> configuration file, or delete old test databases you no longer need via MongoDB Compass.</p></li></ul><h2 data-path-to-node="17">3. The Windows Culprits (The Automatic Fillers)</h2><p data-path-to-node="18">If it isn't your code, Windows is likely hoarding files automatically in the background via these hidden spots:</p><ul data-path-to-node="19"><li><p data-path-to-node="19,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="19,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Windows Update Cache:</b> Windows downloads updates in the background and keeps the old files "just in case."</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="19,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="19,1,0" data-index-in-node="0">System Restore Points:</b> Windows automatically creates backups of system files every time a major change happens. These can take up tens of gigabytes.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="19,2,0"><b data-path-to-node="19,2,0" data-index-in-node="0">Vite / Browser Temp Files:</b> As you develop and test your frontend apps in Vite, your browser and system create massive amounts of local cache and temp data.</p></li></ul><h2 data-path-to-node="21">üõ†Ô∏è How to quickly reclaim your space right now</h2><p data-path-to-node="22">Instead of guessing where the space is going, let's find it and delete it.</p><h3 data-path-to-node="23">Step 1: Run Windows Storage Sense</h3><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="24"><li><p data-path-to-node="24,0,0">Press the <b data-path-to-node="24,0,0" data-index-in-node="10">Windows Key</b>, type <b data-path-to-node="24,0,0" data-index-in-node="28">Storage settings</b>, and hit Enter.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="24,1,0">Turn on <b data-path-to-node="24,1,0" data-index-in-node="8">Storage Sense</b> (it will automatically clear temporary files for you).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="24,2,0">Click on <b data-path-to-node="24,2,0" data-index-in-node="9">Temporary files</b>, wait for it to scan, and click <b data-path-to-node="24,2,0" data-index-in-node="57">Remove files</b> (this safely deletes old Windows updates and system trash).</p></li></ol><h3 data-path-to-node="25">Step 2: Use a Visual Disk Analyzer (Highly Recommended)</h3><p data-path-to-node="26">Download a free, lightweight tool like <b data-path-to-node="26" data-index-in-node="39">WizTree</b> or <b data-path-to-node="26" data-index-in-node="50">WinDirStat</b>.</p><ul data-path-to-node="27"><li><p data-path-to-node="27,0,0">These tools scan your C drive in under a minute and show you a visual map of exactly which folders are taking up the most space.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="27,1,0">If a rogue <code data-path-to-node="27,1,0" data-index-in-node="11">AppData</code> folder or an old MongoDB log file is taking up 40GB, you will spot it instantly.</p></li></ul><p data-path-to-node="28">Have you noticed your drive dropping by gigabytes suddenly while running certain commands, or has it just been a slow build-up over time?</p></div></message-content><!----></div></structured-content-container><!----><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" class="response-footer complete is-mobile gap"><!----><!----><!----><sources-list _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" class="sources-list ng-star-inserted" style=""><!----></sources-list><!----><election-info-disclaimer _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" _nghost-ng-c3453717024="" style="display: none;" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></election-info-disclaimer><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div></div><!----><!----><sensitive-memories-banner _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" _nghost-ng-c1048235422="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></sensitive-memories-banner><!----><!----><!----><!----></div></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c4131263072="" class="response-container-footer ng-tns-c4131263072-13 ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><message-actions _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" footer="" class="hide-on-print ng-tns-c1256094186-14 hide-action-bar ng-tns-c4131263072-13 ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c1256094186=""><div _ngcontent-ng-c1256094186="" class="actions-container-v2 ng-tns-c1256094186-14 mobile"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1256094186="" class="buttons-container-v2 ng-tns-c1256094186-14 ng-star-inserted"><thumb-up-button _ngcontent-ng-c1256094186="" _nghost-ng-c4269877486="" class="ng-tns-c1256094186-14 luminous-theme ng-star-inserted"><gem-icon-button _ngcontent-ng-c4269877486="" tabindex="-1" theme="lm" type="onSurface" arialabel="Good response" gemtooltip="G