tts ng-trigger ng-trigger-singleResponseEnter ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c4131263072="" class="single-draft-response-container ng-tns-c4131263072-19"><!----></div></div><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c4131263072="" class="response-container-header-status ng-tns-c4131263072-19"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c4131263072="" class="response-container-header-processing-state ng-tns-c4131263072-19"></div></div></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c4131263072="" class="presented-response-container ng-tns-c4131263072-19" jslog="283401;track:impression,attention" data-hveid="2"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c4131263072="" class="response-container-content ng-tns-c4131263072-19 is-mobile"><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" class="response-content ng-tns-c4131263072-19"><!----><thinking-overlay _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" _nghost-ng-c3909110362="" class="enable-luminous-fast-follows ng-star-inserted"><!----></thinking-overlay><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" class="model-response-label-announcer" aria-live="off" aria-busy="false"><!----><!----><h2 _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" class="cdk-visually-hidden screen-reader-model-response-label ng-star-inserted" style=""> Gemini said </h2><!----><!----></div><!----><structured-content-container _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" class="model-response-text is-mobile processing-state-visible ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c1632122541="" style="height: auto;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1632122541="" class="container"><message-content _ngcontent-ng-c1632122541="" _nghost-ng-c2728394718="" id="message-content-id-r_5824fdd1d4a7d382" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2728394718="" inline-copy-host="" class="markdown markdown-main-panel enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color tutor-markdown-rendering" id="model-response-message-contentr_5824fdd1d4a7d382" aria-busy="false" aria-live="off" dir="ltr" style="--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: ease-out;"><p data-path-to-node="0">Perfect, knowing you're on Windows 10 makes this much easier because Windows 10 gives us direct access to the classic Group Policy Editor and Settings layout. We can use this to hard-lock these background services so Windows can't sneakily turn them back on during a reboot.</p><p data-path-to-node="1">Let's completely shut down Delivery Optimization and Windows Update background hogs using Windows 10's specific native tools.</p><h2 data-path-to-node="3">üõ†Ô∏è Step 1: Force Delivery Optimization Off via Group Policy</h2><p data-path-to-node="4">If you are using <b data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="17">Windows 10 Pro or Enterprise</b>, this is the absolute most powerful way to kill it because Group Policy overrides regular settings.</p><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="5"><li><p data-path-to-node="5,0,0">Press <code data-path-to-node="5,0,0" data-index-in-node="6">Win + R</code>, type <code data-path-to-node="5,0,0" data-index-in-node="20">gpedit.msc</code>, and press <b data-path-to-node="5,0,0" data-index-in-node="42">Enter</b>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="5,1,0">In the left sidebar, navigate down this path:
<code data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="46">Computer Configuration</code> &gt; <code data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="71">Administrative Templates</code> &gt; <code data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="98">Windows Components</code> &gt; <code data-path-to-node="5,1,0" data-index-in-node="119">Delivery Optimization</code></p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="5,2,0">On the right side, find the policy named <b data-path-to-node="5,2,0" data-index-in-node="41">Download Mode</b> and double-click it.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="5,3,0">Set it to <b data-path-to-node="5,3,0" data-index-in-node="10">Enabled</b>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="5,4,0">Under the <i data-path-to-node="5,4,0" data-index-in-node="10">Options</i> dropdown below, change the Download Mode to <b data-path-to-node="5,4,0" data-index-in-node="62">Bypass (100)</b> or <b data-path-to-node="5,4,0" data-index-in-node="78">Simple (99)</b> depending on your exact sub-version. (Setting it to <i data-path-to-node="5,4,0" data-index-in-node="142">Bypass</i> forces Windows to completely bypass Delivery Optimization and use standard HTTP infrastructure instead of P2P).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="5,5,0">Click <b data-path-to-node="5,5,0" data-index-in-node="6">Apply</b> and <b data-path-to-node="5,5,0" data-index-in-node="16">OK</b>.</p></li></ol><blockquote data-path-to-node="6"><p data-path-to-node="6,0">üí° <i data-path-to-node="6,0" data-index-in-node="3">Note: If you are on Windows 10 Home, you won't have <code data-path-to-node="6,0" data-index-in-node="55">gpedit.msc</code>. Skip this step and rely on the Registry edit from my previous message instead‚Äîit achieves the exact same thing.</i></p></blockquote><h2 data-path-to-node="8">üõ†Ô∏è Step 2: Set Your Wi-Fi/Ethernet to "Metered Connection"</h2><p data-path-to-node="9">This is a brilliant Windows 10 trick that every developer should use. When you tell Windows your network is "metered" (like a limited mobile hotspot), it immediately freezes all non-essential background downloading, including major updates and delivery optimization sharing.</p><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="10"><li><p data-path-to-node="10,0,0">Click your <b data-path-to-node="10,0,0" data-index-in-node="11">Wi-Fi or Network icon</b> in the bottom right corner of your taskbar.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="10,1,0">Click on <b data-path-to-node="10,1,0" data-index-in-node="9">Properties</b> under the network you are currently connected to.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="10,2,0">Scroll down until you see <b data-path-to-node="10,2,0" data-index-in-node="26">Metered connection</b>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="10,3,0">Toggle the switch to <b data-path-to-node="10,3,0" data-index-in-node="21">ON</b> under "Set as metered connection".</p></li></ol><p data-path-to-node="11"><i data-path-to-node="11" data-index-in-node="0">(Don't worry‚Äîthis won't slow down your NPM installs or browser speeds. It just strictly tells Windows components: "Stop downloading things without asking me first.")</i></p><h2 data-path-to-node="13">üõ†Ô∏è Step 3: Turn Off Background Apps</h2><p data-path-to-node="14">Windows 10 runs dozens of built-in apps in the background that constantly look for updates and write cache data to your C Drive.</p><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="15"><li><p data-path-to-node="15,0,0">Open your Windows 10 <b data-path-to-node="15,0,0" data-index-in-node="21">Settings</b> (<code data-path-to-node="15,0,0" data-index-in-node="31">Win + I</code>).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="15,1,0">Go to <b data-path-to-node="15,1,0" data-index-in-node="6">Privacy</b> &gt; scroll down the left menu to <b data-path-to-node="15,1,0" data-index-in-node="45">Background apps</b>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="15,2,0">Toggle the main switch at the top <b data-path-to-node="15,2,0" data-index-in-node="34">"Let apps run in the background"</b> to <b data-path-to-node="15,2,0" data-index-in-node="70">OFF</b>.</p></li></ol><p data-path-to-node="17">Between the updated <code data-path-to-node="17" data-index-in-node="20">.bat</code> cleaner script we created earlier, setting your connection to metered, and locking down the group policy, your computer will finally feel like a fast, quiet development machine again instead of an updating server!</p></div></message-content><!----></div></structured-content-container><!----><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" class="response-footer complete is-mobile gap"><!----><!----><!----><sources-list _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" class="sources-list ng-star-inserted" style=""><!----></sources-list><!----><election-info-disclaimer _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" _nghost-ng-c3453717024="" style="display: none;" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></election-info-disclaimer><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div></div><!----><!----><sensitive-memories-banner _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" _nghost-ng-c1048235422="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></sensitive-memories-banner><!----><!----><!----><!----></div></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c4131263072="" class="response-container-footer ng-tns-c4131263072-19 ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><message-actions _ngcontent-ng-c1916596297="" footer="" class="hide-on-print ng-tns-c1256094186-20 hide-action-bar ng-tns-c4131263072-19 ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c1256094186=""><div _ngcontent-ng-c1256094186="" class="actions-container-v2 ng-tns-c1256094186-20 mobile"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1256094186="" class="buttons-container-v2 ng-tns-c1256094186-20 ng-star-inserted"><thumb-up-button _ngcontent-ng-c1256094186="" _nghost-ng-c4269877486="" class="ng-tns-c1256094186-20 luminous-theme ng-star-inserted"><gem-icon-button _ngcontent-ng-c4269877486="" tabindex="-1" theme="lm" type="onSurface" arialabel="Good response" gemtooltip="Good response" data-test-id="thumb-up-button" class="mat-mdc-tooltip-trigger gem-button gem-button-badge-size-